                                                "text": "Sunning himself on the board steps, I saw for the first time Mr. Farquhar Fenelon Cooke.[…]A silver snaffle on a heavy leather watch guard which connected the pockets of his corduroy waistcoat, together with a huge gold stirrup in his Ascot tie, sufficiently proclaimed his tastes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "595ef749-5302-4732-ab64-b6919847cd13",
                                                "sense_id": "57bafd4b-4272-30ee-88b8-3cb3ff75f084",
                                                "text": "You have seen it for yourselves in the play by Aristophanes, where Socrates goes whirling round, proclaiming that he is walking on air, and uttering a great deal of other nonsense about things of which I know nothing whatsoever."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54d7ed93-274e-3ea2-ad07-a93761df6343",
                                        "entry_id": "b95dd0a1-f9a6-36a5-a64f-36d9df2b6ce0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make (something) the subject of an official proclamation bringing it within the scope of emergency powers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f549b902-21e0-4fb1-b46c-bb31003a7ee3",
                                                "sense_id": "54d7ed93-274e-3ea2-ad07-a93761df6343",
                                                "text": "Were those baronies proclaimed at the time you were in them? –Some of them are; the barony of Duhallow is proclaimed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48b9eaaa-6a9b-439e-b260-de118def50a7",
                                                "sense_id": "54d7ed93-274e-3ea2-ad07-a93761df6343",
                                                "text": "… the Magistrates present, naturally excited by the occurrence, applied to Government to proclaim the baronies in which the outrage had occurred …"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c1e5569-6210-4768-808b-d53a3fbba979",
                                                "sense_id": "54d7ed93-274e-3ea2-ad07-a93761df6343",
                                                "text": "In due course the Dáil was proclaimed, fruitless efforts were made to suppress it and all its institutions, including, of course, the IRA."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c7563cda-a341-4b38-9d57-85c4a9de5241",
                        "source_entry_id": "e4159f6b-7baf-3788-964e-4eaf3e38be73",
                        "target_lang_word": "promulgate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "promulgate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5938699-9adf-3ff1-8423-0c5e74d27880",
                                        "entry_id": "3c87d6c4-d4a1-384f-8cdc-c1394744ae89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make known or make public."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32b4d9c6-d23d-445b-91fd-1b6f177f445a",
                                                "sense_id": "c5938699-9adf-3ff1-8423-0c5e74d27880",
                                                "text": "’Tis yet to know, / Which when I know, that boaſting is an Honour, / I ſhall promulgate. I fetch by life and being, / From Men of Royall Seige."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4261136d-9784-409c-9c65-07656bd47a3c",
                                                "sense_id": "c5938699-9adf-3ff1-8423-0c5e74d27880",
                                                "text": "Prieſts have invented, and the world admir’d / What knaviſh prieſts promulgate as inſpir’d ; / ’Till reaſon, now no longer overaw’d, / Reſumes her pow’rs, and ſpurns the clumſy fraud ; / And, common-ſenſe diffuſing real day, / The meteor of the goſpel dies away !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a8ef635-1bc7-32b1-929e-b4c005fc0d11",
                                        "entry_id": "3c87d6c4-d4a1-384f-8cdc-c1394744ae89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put into effect as a regulation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6072cb2a-e4f4-4636-ae17-1d4647aa6db5",
                                                "sense_id": "0a8ef635-1bc7-32b1-929e-b4c005fc0d11",
                                                "text": "[…] the Statute of Uses was delayed until 1536 and the Statute of Wills until 1540, but both statutes were promulgated in 1532, and formed part of a policy which we may compare, not favourably, with the of Edward I[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7616bb0f-4fa2-3446-9c70-5bbb8ca048e3",
                                        "entry_id": "3c87d6c4-d4a1-384f-8cdc-c1394744ae89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To advocate on behalf of (something or someone, especially of an idea); to spread knowledge of and make more widely known."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "nonstandard",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7d1244cf-e0f4-479b-a909-10b982f0e293",
                        "source_entry_id": "e4159f6b-7baf-3788-964e-4eaf3e38be73",
                        "target_lang_word": "declare",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "declare",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b691aff-d999-3b49-8ca4-bd4cbd112161",
                                        "entry_id": "4b200412-e3cb-30eb-85e1-4d323e469f0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make clear, explain, interpret."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0679dc5-be8a-4619-adc0-38c0431ce734",
                                                "sense_id": "2b691aff-d999-3b49-8ca4-bd4cbd112161",
                                                "text": "Then answered Peter and sayd to him: declare unto us thys parable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f15c2f0c-a0e3-4a7a-8ba5-5af5f8e2d741",
                                                "sense_id": "2b691aff-d999-3b49-8ca4-bd4cbd112161",
                                                "text": "To declare this a little, vve muſt aſſume, that the Surfaces of all ſuch Bodies, […] are exactly ſmooth only in a popular, or at moſt in a Phyſical ſenſe, but not in a ſtrict and rigid ſenſe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d8d3580-7457-3c89-ba34-98f82a0f0c81",
                                        "entry_id": "4b200412-e3cb-30eb-85e1-4d323e469f0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To assert or announce formally, officially, explicitly, or emphatically."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efa354f9-9bad-4952-b25c-998e95e71db0",
                                                "sense_id": "6d8d3580-7457-3c89-ba34-98f82a0f0c81",
                                                "text": "He declared him innocent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9edc103e-f646-40cb-8e8d-1cf453aedfd0",
                                                "sense_id": "6d8d3580-7457-3c89-ba34-98f82a0f0c81",
                                                "text": "declare bankruptcy"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e2c8610-e3c2-4bfc-9a58-272cefc5c303",
                                                "sense_id": "6d8d3580-7457-3c89-ba34-98f82a0f0c81",
                                                "text": "declare victory"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42fd79d4-d6a2-462d-a2df-723b4effcf9d",
                                                "sense_id": "6d8d3580-7457-3c89-ba34-98f82a0f0c81",
                                                "text": "declare war"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa4ed19a-ac6d-47ba-8f66-05de8c48eab3",
                                                "sense_id": "6d8d3580-7457-3c89-ba34-98f82a0f0c81",
                                                "text": "One South Korean opposition party called on Moon to declare the current air pollution problem a national disaster."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85e8555a-b0cd-4d1c-aabb-abea0c3ff43c",
                                                "sense_id": "6d8d3580-7457-3c89-ba34-98f82a0f0c81",
                                                "text": "declare an innings closed"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "304705bc-d3c7-36a8-91cb-383e2b2ced25",
                                        "entry_id": "4b200412-e3cb-30eb-85e1-4d323e469f0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To inform government customs or taxation officials of goods one is importing or of income, expenses, or other circumstances affecting one's taxes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f596e0e3-e9e7-4604-87a5-9bbc0d2e3b78",
                                                "sense_id": "304705bc-d3c7-36a8-91cb-383e2b2ced25",
                                                "text": "The prosecution has introduced evidence, including canceled checks, to show that the judge failed to declare part of his income."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b80d2e5-8e2c-3fbf-b6c4-b91f1b73e8fd",
                                        "entry_id": "4b200412-e3cb-30eb-85e1-4d323e469f0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To show one's cards in order to score."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b63d17a-75aa-3061-ac06-50f8a20cec88",
                                        "entry_id": "4b200412-e3cb-30eb-85e1-4d323e469f0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "For a constituency in an election to officially announce the result"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c37c495-f8ab-4768-a8ca-a128e4b0ad88",
                                                "sense_id": "2b63d17a-75aa-3061-ac06-50f8a20cec88",
                                                "text": "Houghton and Sunderland South was the first constituency to declare in the 2015 general election."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1220772-e587-31ce-b627-36e35bcf8088",
                                        "entry_id": "4b200412-e3cb-30eb-85e1-4d323e469f0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The decision of the captain to let the bowling side bat in test cricket to save time without being all out."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6926377c-7946-4aca-8886-8dfc188be76e",
                                                "sense_id": "b1220772-e587-31ce-b627-36e35bcf8088",
                                                "text": "He declared at 689-7."
                                            }
